    >
        <h1 dir="auto">GitHub Copilot FAQ</h1>
<p dir="auto">Your complete guide to using GitHub Copilot effectively. Whether you're just getting started, troubleshooting issues, or exploring advanced features, you'll find answers and resources here.</p>
<blockquote>
<p dir="auto"><strong>Note</strong><br>
Last updated: January 9, 2026 | For real-time Copilot status, check <a href="https://githubstatus.com/" rel="nofollow">GitHub's Status page</a></p>
</blockquote>
<hr>
<h2 dir="auto">Quick Start</h2>
<p dir="auto">New to GitHub Copilot? Start here:</p>
<p dir="auto"><strong>Getting Started with Copilot:</strong></p>
<ol dir="auto">
<li>Choose your plan (Free, Pro, Business, or Enterprise)</li>
<li>Install the extension for your IDE (<a href="https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=GitHub.copilot" rel="nofollow">VS Code</a>, <a href="https://visualstudio.microsoft.com/" rel="nofollow">Visual Studio</a>, <a href="https://plugins.jetbrains.com/plugin/17718-github-copilot" rel="nofollow">JetBrains IDEs</a>, or others)</li>
<li>Sign in with your GitHub account</li>
<li>Start coding—Copilot will suggest completions and answer questions</li>
</ol>
<p dir="auto"><strong>Quick Resources:</strong></p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><a href="https://github.blog/developer-skills/github/what-can-github-copilot-do-examples/" rel="nofollow">What can GitHub Copilot do?</a> - Real-world examples</li>
<li><a href="https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/">How to use GitHub Copilot</a> - Official documentation</li>
<li><a href="https://github.com/features/copilot#:~:text=Frequently%20asked%20questions">GitHub Copilot FAQs</a> - General questions answered</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<hr>
<h2 dir="auto">Choose Your Plan</h2>
<p dir="auto"><strong>Copilot Free</strong> - Limited access, no credit card required</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Up to 2,000 code completions per month</li>
<li>Up to 50 messages per month in Copilot Chat</li>
<li>Available in VS Code</li>
<li><a href="https://github.blog/news-insights/product-news/github-copilot-in-vscode-free/" rel="nofollow">Learn more</a></li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto"><strong>Copilot Pro</strong> - Full access for individuals ($20/month)</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Unlimited code completions and Chat messages</li>
<li>GPT-4, Claude, and Gemini models</li>
<li>Early access to new features</li>
<li>Available in VS Code, Visual Studio, JetBrains, Xcode, and more</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto"><strong>Copilot Business</strong> - Team collaboration and org-wide management</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Everything in Pro</li>
<li>Organization policies and controls</li>
<li>Usage tracking and insights</li>
<li><a href="https://github.com/enterprise/contact">Contact sales</a></li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto"><strong>Copilot Enterprise</strong> - Full AI development platform for organizations</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>All Business features</li>
<li>Custom models trained on your codebase</li>
<li>Code search and repository indexing</li>
<li><a href="https://github.com/enterprise/contact">Contact sales</a></li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto"><strong>Free for Students &amp; Teachers</strong></p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Full Copilot Pro access</li>
<li>Verify through <a href="https://education.github.com/">GitHub Education</a></li>
<li>Includes Copilot Coding Agent (new!)</li>
<li><a href="https://docs.github.com/en/education/explore-the-benefits-of-teaching-and-learning-with-github-education">Apply now</a></li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2 dir="auto">Copilot Free</h2>
<p dir="auto">GitHub Copilot Free provides limited access to select Copilot features, allowing you to experience AI-powered coding assistance without a subscription.</p>
<p dir="auto"><strong>Key Features:</strong></p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Up to 2,000 code completions in IDEs per month</li>
<li>Up to 50 premium requests per month</li>
<li>Limited access to Copilot Chat (50 chats per month)</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto">For more details, see the announcement <a href="https://github.com/orgs/community/discussions/147189">Introducing GitHub Copilot Free</a>. Visit the <a href="https://github.com/copilot">immersive experience</a> and <a href="https://gh.io/copilot-free-blog" rel="nofollow">announcement blog</a>. Read the comprehensive <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/managing-copilot/managing-copilot-as-an-individual-subscriber/about-github-copilot-free">FAQs on GitHub Docs</a>.</p>
<p dir="auto"><strong>Education Note:</strong> If you had Copilot Free and are now a verified student or teacher, learn how to <a href="https://github.com/orgs/community/discussions/111352#enable-copilot-education">transfer to Copilot Pro</a>. The Copilot Coding Agent is now available to all GitHub Education students and educators.</p>
<p dir="auto">See also: <a href="https://github.blog/developer-skills/github/what-can-github-copilot-do-examples/" rel="nofollow">How to use GitHub Copilot: What it can do and real-world examples</a></p>
<hr>
<hr>
<h2 dir="auto">Getting Help</h2>
<h3 dir="auto">Quick Troubleshooting</h3>
<p dir="auto"><strong>Copilot isn't working?</strong></p>
<ol dir="auto">
<li>Check <a href="https://githubstatus.com/" rel="nofollow">GitHub's Status page</a> for service incidents</li>
<li>Verify you have a valid subscription or are using Copilot Free</li>
<li>Restart your IDE</li>
<li>Reinstall the Copilot extension</li>
</ol>
<p dir="auto"><strong>Still having issues?</strong></p>
<h3 dir="auto">Common Issues and Solutions</h3>
<h4 dir="auto">Extension Issues</h4>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><a href="https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/troubleshooting-github-copilot/troubleshooting-common-issues-with-github-copilot#unable-to-use-the-github-copilot-extension-in-the-ide">Unable to use the GitHub Copilot extension</a></li>
<li><a href="https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/troubleshooting-github-copilot/troubleshooting-common-issues-with-github-copilot#github-copilot-not-working-in-some-files">GitHub Copilot not working in some files</a></li>
<li><a href="https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/troubleshooting-github-copilot/troubleshooting-common-issues-with-github-copilot#github-copilot-content-exclusions-are-not-being-applied">Content exclusions not being applied</a></li>
<li><a href="https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/troubleshooting-github-copilot/troubleshooting-common-issues-with-github-copilot#error-github-copilot-could-not-connect-to-server-extension-activation-failed">Connection and activation errors</a></li>
<li><a href="https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/troubleshooting-github-copilot/troubleshooting-common-issues-with-github-copilot#github-copilot-not-suggesting-multiple-lines-of-code">Multi-line code suggestions not working</a></li>
</ul>
<h4 dir="auto">Network and Firewall</h4>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><a href="https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/troubleshooting-github-copilot/troubleshooting-network-errors-for-github-copilot#diagnosing-network-issues">Diagnosing network issues</a></li>
<li><a href="https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/troubleshooting-github-copilot/troubleshooting-network-errors-for-github-copilot#troubleshooting-proxy-errors">Troubleshooting proxy errors</a></li>
<li><a href="https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/troubleshooting-github-copilot/troubleshooting-network-errors-for-github-copilot#troubleshooting-certificate-related-errors">Troubleshooting certificate errors</a></li>
</ul>
<h4 dir="auto">Copilot Chat Issues</h4>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><a href="https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/troubleshooting-github-copilot/troubleshooting-issues-with-github-copilot-chat-in-ides#troubleshooting-issues-caused-by-version-incompatibility">Version incompatibility issues</a></li>
<li><a href="https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/troubleshooting-github-copilot/troubleshooting-issues-with-github-copilot-chat-in-ides#troubleshooting-authentication-issues-in-your-editor">Authentication issues in editors</a></li>
<li><a href="https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/troubleshooting-github-copilot/troubleshooting-issues-with-github-copilot-chat-in-ides#error-oops-your-response-got-filtered">Response filtering errors</a></li>
<li><a href="https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/troubleshooting-github-copilot/troubleshooting-issues-with-copilot-spaces">Copilot Spaces loading issues</a></li>
</ul>
<h3 dir="auto">Billing &amp; Subscriptions</h3>
<p dir="auto"><strong>Getting a refund:</strong><br>
We offer self-serve refunds for Copilot. Visit the <a href="https://support.github.com/contact/account?flow=refund_copilot_individual">Help with your account</a> section.</p>
<p dir="auto">The Virtual Agent can often provide immediate refunds. If your concern isn't resolved, use the contact form to reach the billing team.</p>
<p dir="auto"><strong>Need help with your subscription?</strong></p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>View your billing information in your <a href="https://github.com/settings/billing">GitHub account settings</a></li>
<li><a href="https://support.github.com/">Contact GitHub Support</a> for billing questions</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2 dir="auto">Troubleshooting</h2>
<hr>
<h2 dir="auto">For Organizations</h2>
<h3 dir="auto">Setting Up Copilot for Your Team</h3>
<p dir="auto"><strong>Copilot Business</strong> - Collaboration and management tools</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><a href="https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/managing-copilot/managing-copilot-business">Enable Copilot for your organization</a></li>
<li>Manage organization policies and controls</li>
<li>Track usage and insights</li>
<li><a href="https://github.blog/news-insights/product-news/github-copilot-meet-the-new-coding-agent/" rel="nofollow">Copilot coding agent for teams</a></li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto"><strong>Copilot Enterprise</strong> - Full platform with custom models</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Everything in Business, plus:</li>
<li>Custom models trained on your codebase</li>
<li>Code search with Copilot</li>
<li>Repository indexing</li>
<li><a href="https://github.com/enterprise/contact">Contact sales</a></li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto"><strong>Network Routing</strong><br>
Copilot requests route through different endpoints based on your subscription:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><a href="https://docs.github.com/en/enterprise-cloud@latest/copilot/managing-copilot/managing-copilot-for-your-enterprise/managing-access-to-copilot-in-your-enterprise/managing-github-copilot-access-to-your-enterprises-network">Learn about subscription-based network routing</a></li>
</ul>
<h3 dir="auto">Key Features for Teams</h3>
<h4 dir="auto">GitHub Copilot Coding Agent</h4>
<p dir="auto">Automate implementation of GitHub issues.</p>
<p dir="auto"><strong>What it does:</strong></p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Simple issue assignment via GitHub.com, GitHub Mobile, or CLI</li>
<li>Automated environment setup with GitHub Actions</li>
<li>Regular progress updates through draft PRs and session logs</li>
<li>Built-in security policies and review requirements</li>
<li>MCP server support for additional context</li>
<li>Vision model support for screenshots and mockups</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto"><strong>Availability:</strong></p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Copilot Enterprise: available now</li>
<li>Copilot Pro+: available now</li>
<li>Copilot Business: available since June 24, 2025</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto"><a href="https://gh.io/copilot-coding-agent-repository-opt-in" rel="nofollow">Get started with the coding agent</a></p>
<h4 dir="auto">Copilot Spaces</h4>
<p dir="auto">Centralize project context for more relevant AI responses.</p>
<p dir="auto"><strong>What it includes:</strong></p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Curated code, documents, and custom instructions</li>
<li>Organization-level spaces for shared expertise</li>
<li>Automatic updates as repositories change</li>
<li>Support for issues and pull requests (as of June 19, 2025)</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2 dir="auto">Latest Features &amp; Updates</h2>
<h3 dir="auto">New in 2025</h3>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>
<p dir="auto"><strong><a href="https://github.blog/changelog/2025-06-25-anthropic-claude-sonnet-4-and-claude-opus-4-are-now-generally-available-in-github-copilot" rel="nofollow">Anthropic Claude Sonnet 4 and Claude Opus 4</a></strong> — Now generally available in GitHub Copilot.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p dir="auto"><strong><a href="https://github.blog/changelog/2025-06-25-improved-attachments-and-larger-context-in-copilot-chat-in-public-preview" rel="nofollow">Improved attachments and larger context in Copilot Chat</a></strong> — In public preview.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p dir="auto"><strong><a href="https://github.blog/changelog/2025-06-23-github-desktop-3-5-github-copilot-commit-message-generation-now-generally-available" rel="nofollow">GitHub Desktop 3.5</a></strong> — Commit message generation now generally available.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 dir="auto">Important: Model Changes</h3>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>
<p dir="auto"><strong><a href="https://github.blog/changelog/2025-06-20-upcoming-deprecation-of-o1-gpt-4-5-o3-mini-and-gpt-4o" rel="nofollow">Upcoming deprecation of o1, GPT-4.5, o3-mini, and GPT-4o</a></strong> — Plan your Copilot usage accordingly. Alternative models available.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p dir="auto"><strong><a href="https://github.blog/changelog/2025-05-07-enforcement-of-copilot-premium-request-limits-coming-soon" rel="nofollow">Enforcement of Copilot premium request limits</a></strong> — Now in effect. Understand your usage patterns.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 dir="auto">Public Preview Features</h3>
<p dir="auto">Try these new capabilities:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>
<p dir="auto"><strong><a href="https://github.blog/changelog/2025-05-19-agent-mode-and-mcp-support-for-copilot-in-jetbrains-eclipse-and-xcode-now-in-public-preview/" rel="nofollow">Agent mode and MCP support for IDEs</a></strong> — JetBrains, Eclipse, and Xcode</p>
</li>
<li>
<p dir="auto"><strong><a href="https://github.blog/changelog/2025-06-19-copilot-spaces-now-support-issues-and-pull-requests-public-preview/" rel="nofollow">Copilot Spaces with issues and PRs</a></strong> — Bring more context to your spaces</p>
</li>
<li>
<p dir="auto"><strong><a href="https://github.blog/github-copilot/code-review-waitlist" rel="nofollow">Copilot-powered code reviews</a></strong> — AI-powered feedback on pull requests</p>
</li>
<li>
<p dir="auto"><strong><a href="https://github.com/features/preview/copilot-autofix-for-dependabot">GitHub Copilot Autofix for Dependabot</a></strong> — Fix breaking changes (TypeScript)</p>
</li>
<li>
<p dir="auto"><strong><a href="https://github.blog/changelog/2025-05-19-github-copilot-app-modernization-for-java-now-in-public-preview/" rel="nofollow">App modernization for Java and .NET</a></strong> — Modernize legacy code</p>
</li>
<li>
<p dir="auto"><strong><a href="https://github.co/copilot-custom-models" rel="nofollow">Copilot fine-tuned models</a></strong> — Models trained on your codebase</p>
</li>
<li>
<p dir="auto"><strong><a href="https://github.com/features/preview/copilot-autofix-for-partners">GitHub Copilot Autofix for Partner Tools</a></strong> — Fix vulnerabilities from partner tools</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto">Note: <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/github-terms/github-pre-release-license-terms">GitHub Pre-release License Terms</a> apply to preview features.</p>
<hr>
<hr>
<h2 dir="auto">AI Models in GitHub Copilot</h2>
<p dir="auto">Choose the right model for your task:</p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table><table role="table">
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Model</th>
<th>Best For</th>
<th>Speed</th>
<th>Cost</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>GPT-4o</strong></td>
<td>General-purpose coding</td>
<td>Fast</td>
<td>Standard</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>o3-mini</strong></td>
<td>Simple, quick tasks</td>
<td>Very Fast</td>
<td>Low</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Gemini 2.0 Flash</strong></td>
<td>Visual analysis (diagrams, UI)</td>
<td>Fast</td>
<td>Standard</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Claude Sonnet 3.5</strong></td>
<td>Everyday coding tasks</td>
<td>Fast</td>
<td>Standard</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Claude Sonnet 3.7</strong></td>
<td>Complex multi-file tasks</td>
<td>Moderate</td>
<td>Standard</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Claude Sonnet 4</strong></td>
<td>Advanced reasoning</td>
<td>Moderate</td>
<td>Standard</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Claude Opus 4</strong></td>
<td>Complex problem-solving</td>
<td>Slower</td>
<td>Higher</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
<p dir="auto"><a href="https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/using-github-copilot/ai-models/comparing-ai-models-using-different-tasks">Compare models with examples</a></p>
<p dir="auto"><strong>Deprecations Coming:</strong> o1, GPT-4.5, o3-mini, and GPT-4o models will be deprecated. Plan your usage accordingly and explore alternatives above.</p>
<hr>
<h2 dir="auto">Security, Privacy &amp; Compliance</h2>
<p dir="auto">We prioritize security, privacy, compliance, and transparency in GitHub Copilot's development.</p>
<p dir="auto"><strong>Key Resources:</strong></p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><a href="https://copilot.github.trust.page/faq" rel="nofollow">GitHub Copilot Trust Center FAQs</a> - Comprehensive answers to trust-related questions</li>
<li><a href="https://github.com/customer-terms/github-copilot-product-specific-terms">Product Specific Terms</a> - Legal terms</li>
<li><a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/github-terms/github-copilot-pre-release-terms">Pre-release Terms</a> - For beta features</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto"><a href="https://github.com/orgs/community/discussions/categories/copilot">Contact GitHub with security questions</a></p>
